# POPF/POPFD/POPFQ -- override
# The manual's Operation for protected, compatibility and 64-bit mode
# (VM = 0): at CPL 0 every flag POPF may change is loaded (IOPL included);
# at 0 < CPL <= IOPL everything but IOPL; at CPL > IOPL neither IOPL nor
# IF. RF is cleared, VM, VIF and VIP are unaffected, and a 16-bit POPF
# leaves the upper half of EFLAGS alone. In real-address mode it is the
# CPL 0 case. Virtual-8086 mode (IOPL < 3: #GP; VME) isn't in v1.
@operation
tmp := Pop();
mask := 247FD5H;
IF CPL > 0 THEN mask := mask AND FFFFCFFFH; FI;
IF CPL > IOPL THEN mask := mask AND FFFFFDFFH; FI;
IF OperandSize = 16 THEN mask := mask AND FFFFH; FI;
StoreFlags(tmp, mask);
SetFlag(RF, 0);
